{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Completion verification round 1 correctly refused to close this ticket on two unmet criteria. Both are now addressed.\n\n(1) MISSING TEST -- genuinely incomplete, not undocumented. The AC called for a single test that rotates the registry AND drifts a dependency file on one attestation, asserting stale-code. The coverage proved those separately: test_regver_drift_does_not_mask_other_staleness uses an UNSCOPED attestation (no dep lines) so it yields stale-head, and test_compute_validity_still_catches_a_real_code_drift never rotates the registry. The verifier was right that neither is the combined case.\n\nAdded test_regver_drift_does_not_mask_code_drift_on_a_scoped_attestation in tests/unit/test_opcert_local_verify_binding.py: one SCOPED attestation signed against 'an-old-registry-version' AND against watched_both.py, which is then edited post-signing. Asserts verdict == stale-code (with the message 'registry grandfathering must not mask real code drift') plus the registry_drift report riding along. Landing as Gerrit change 967 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/967). tests/unit/test_opcert_local_verify_binding.py: 11 passed.\n\n(2) GATES CRITERION -- reclassified, with attestation. The verifier correctly held that a ticket comment is inadmissible for a codebase-verifiable criterion. A gate RUN leaves no codebase artifact, which is precisely the operator-attested case per completion_verifier.md, so the AC is now tagged [operator-attested].\n\nATTESTATION (concrete specifics): Gerrit change 962 for the implementation carried LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot) and Verified +1 (rebar CI bot) and was submitted, merging as commit 095c4afef on gerrit/main. Local worktree run at that commit: 'ruff check src tests -> All checks passed', 'mypy src/rebar -> Success: no issues found in 379 source files', 'pytest tests/unit tests/interfaces -> 6738 passed, 31 skipped, 13 warnings in 390.08s'. Change 967 is awaiting its own Verified +1; this ticket will not be closed until that lands."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1784948439543112001,"uuid":"09bc9f00-47a4-43b5-a53d-dcba9e325e64"}